---
import BlockLayout from '../../layouts/BlockLayout.astro';
import { CHANNELS } from '../../lib/channels';
import { BURN_OFF_DEFINITION } from '../../lib/burnoff';
import { MARINE_ORACLE } from '../../../functions/_lib/oracles/marine-layer';
import { oracleEndpoints } from '../../../functions/_lib/oracles/index';

const title = 'The Marine Layer Oracle: did the sky over El Segundo open?';
const description = 'A paid x402 oracle for El Segundo coastal stratus: did the marine layer burn off on a given morning, and when. Judged from KLAX hourly reports with the rule /marine-layer publishes, with raw METARs, sources, a final flag, and a signed attestation. 0.01 USDC. Any date since 2000.';
const esc = CHANNELS.ESC;
const ep = oracleEndpoints(MARINE_ORACLE as never);
const example = MARINE_ORACLE.discovery.output.example;
const curl = `curl -X POST ${ep.etherlink.url} -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H 'Idempotency-Key: <stable-request-id>' -H 'Payment-Signature: <base64-x402-v2>' --data '{"date":"2026-09-23"}'`;
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebAPI', name: 'The Marine Layer Oracle', description, url: 'https://pointcast.xyz/oracles/marine-layer',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0.01', priceCurrency: 'USD' }, provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PointCast', url: 'https://pointcast.xyz' },
};
---

<BlockLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <main class="mlo" style={`--c50:${esc.color50};--c600:${esc.color600};--c800:${esc.color800}`}>
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">PointCast</a><span>/</span><a href="/oracles">oracles</a><span>/</span><span>marine layer</span></nav>
    <header class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">THE MARINE LAYER ORACLE · KLAX · 0.01 USDC</p>
      <h1>Did the sky open?</h1>
      <p class="dek">Most summer mornings, and plenty of others, El Segundo wakes up under a grey lid of coastal stratus. This oracle says whether it burned off on a given day and when, using the same rule as <a href="/marine-layer">/marine-layer</a>. It works for any morning since 2000. Every answer carries the hourly reports it was judged from, and it's marked final only when no later report can change it.</p>
      <p class="now" id="now" aria-live="polite">Checking the sky…</p>
    </header>

    <section class="sec" aria-label="What you get">
      <p class="kicker">WHAT ONE CENT BUYS</p>
      <ul class="list">
        <li><b>A verdict:</b> opened (with the time), never opened, no layer, or no record. For this morning it's <em>watching</em> until the window closes.</li>
        <li><b>A final flag</b> you can settle on. It's true only once the morning is over, or once the opening has held for two hours.</li>
        <li><b>The evidence:</b> every hourly KLAX report in the window with its raw METAR, the lowest ceiling, sunrise, and the source URLs.</li>
        <li><b>A signed attestation</b> from the town treasury key, so an agent can cite it later.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" aria-label="Two rails">
      <p class="kicker">TWO RAILS · SAME ANSWER</p>
      <div class="rails">
        <div><b>Etherlink · open now</b><code>{ep.etherlink.method} {ep.etherlink.url}</code><span>Body <code>{'{"date":"YYYY-MM-DD"}'}</code>, or empty for today. Send an Idempotency-Key.</span></div>
        <div><b>Base · x402 Bazaar</b><code>{ep.base.method} {ep.base.url}?date=YYYY-MM-DD</code><span>Any stock x402 client. <em id="base-state">Checking status…</em></span></div>
      </div>
      <pre class="code">{curl}</pre>
      <p class="fine">If NOAA or the Iowa State archive is down or rate-limiting, the oracle answers <code>503 oracle_unavailable</code> before any payment settles. You're never charged for an answer the town couldn't check.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" aria-label="The rule">
      <p class="kicker">THE RULE, IN WORDS</p>
      <ol class="steps">{BURN_OFF_DEFINITION.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}</ol>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" aria-label="Sample">
      <p class="kicker">SAMPLE ANSWER · TRIMMED</p>
      <pre class="code">{JSON.stringify(example, null, 2)}</pre>
    </section>

    <p class="foot"><a href="/marine-layer">a year of mornings, free</a> · <a href="/oracles">all oracles</a> · <a href="/oracles.json">oracles.json</a> · observations: NOAA, public domain</p>
  </main>
</BlockLayout>

<script>
  const now = document.getElementById('now');
  fetch('/api/agent/marine-layer?preview=1').then((r) => r.json()).then((d) => {
    if (!now) return;
    if (d.ok === false) { now.textContent = 'The sources are not answering right now.'; return; }
    const at = d.observedAt ? new Date(d.observedAt).toLocaleTimeString('en-US', { timeZone: 'America/Los_Angeles', hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' }) : '';
    now.textContent = d.underTheLayerNow === true
      ? `Right now: under the layer (KLAX ${at}). Whether and when it opens is the paid answer.`
      : d.underTheLayerNow === false
        ? `Right now: no low deck over KLAX (${at}).`
        : 'No recent report from KLAX.';
  }).catch(() => { if (now) now.textContent = ''; });
  const baseState = document.getElementById('base-state');
  fetch('/api/oracle/marine-layer').then((r) => {
    if (!baseState) return;
    baseState.textContent = r.status === 402 ? 'Status: open.' : r.status === 503 ? 'Status: waiting on the operator to add the CDP key.' : `Status: ${r.status}.`;
  }).catch(() => { if (baseState) baseState.textContent = ''; });
</script>

<style>
  .mlo{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px 18px 96px;color:var(--pc-ink)}
  .crumb{display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:center;padding:6px 0 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--pc-rule);font:10px var(--pc-font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}
  .crumb a{color:var(--pc-ink)}
  .kicker{margin:0 0 12px;font:500 10px var(--pc-font-mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--c800)}
  .hero{padding:44px 0 8px;max-width:880px}
  .hero h1{margin:0;font:500 clamp(40px,6.4vw,76px)/.96 var(--pc-font-sans);letter-spacing:-.035em}
  .dek{margin:18px 0 0;font:400 17px/1.55 var(--pc-font-sans);color:var(--pc-ink-soft)}
  .dek a,.fine a,.foot a{color:var(--c800)}
  .now{margin:16px 0 0;padding:12px 14px;border-left:4px solid var(--c600);background:var(--c50);font:500 15px/1.4 var(--pc-font-sans)}
  .sec{padding-top:44px}
  .list{margin:0;padding-left:20px;max-width:880px;font:400 15px/1.6 var(--pc-font-sans);color:var(--pc-ink-soft)}
  .list li{margin-bottom:8px}.list b{color:var(--pc-ink)}.list em{font-style:normal;color:var(--c800)}
  .rails{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border:1.5px solid var(--c600)}
  .rails>div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;padding:16px;font:400 14px/1.55 var(--pc-font-sans);color:var(--pc-ink-soft)}
  .rails>div+div{border-left:1.5px solid var(--c600)}
  .rails b{font:500 11px var(--pc-font-mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--c800)}
  .rails em{font-style:normal;color:var(--c800)}
  code{font:400 12.5px var(--pc-font-mono);word-break:break-all;color:var(--pc-ink)}
  .code{margin:12px 0 0;padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--pc-rule);background:var(--c50);font:400 12px/1.5 var(--pc-font-mono);white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word}
  .steps{margin:0;padding-left:20px;max-width:880px;font:400 15px/1.6 var(--pc-font-sans);color:var(--pc-ink-soft)}
  .steps li{margin-bottom:8px}
  .fine{margin:12px 0 0;max-width:780px;font:400 12.5px/1.55 var(--pc-font-sans);color:var(--pc-ink-muted)}
  .foot{margin:40px 0 0;font:400 10px/1.8 var(--pc-font-mono);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--pc-ink-muted)}
  @media(max-width:820px){.rails{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rails>div+div{border-left:0;border-top:1.5px solid var(--c600)}.hero{padding-top:28px}}
</style>
